1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,111
The ticket is closed.

2
00:00:02,111 --> 00:00:04,500
The mistake is still live.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,446
The bottle looks included.

4
00:00:07,446 --> 00:00:10,254
The page promises waterproof protection.

5
00:00:10,254 --> 00:00:12,500
The specification says otherwise.

6
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:18,047
Pagemi turns customer confusion into
evidence-linked page repairs.

7
00:00:18,047 --> 00:00:23,500
Here is the working prototype, running on
Google Cloud.

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:29,569
Gemini reads feedback, merchant
specifications, and the product image.

9
00:00:29,569 --> 00:00:31,955
Feedback identifies a problem.

10
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:34,938
The specification supports product facts.

11
00:00:34,938 --> 00:00:41,500
An image can show a bottle, but cannot
prove waterproof performance.

12
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:47,606
The agent separates page problems from
missing information and operational

13
00:00:47,606 --> 00:00:48,147
issues.

14
00:00:48,147 --> 00:00:54,094
It corrects the unsupported waterproof
claim, asks for laptop dimensions, and

15
00:00:54,094 --> 00:00:59,500
leaves a broken zipper or late delivery
for human action.

16
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,742
Each proposed change shows its source.

17
00:01:03,742 --> 00:01:08,465
A separate Gemini request checks the
replacement text.

18
00:01:08,465 --> 00:01:12,597
Program rules restrict edits to three
fields.

19
00:01:12,597 --> 00:01:17,910
Price, inventory, policies, and
certifications stay outside the editing

20
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:18,500
scope.

21
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:24,622
Approval applies to exact wording and
exact evidence.

22
00:01:24,622 --> 00:01:31,400
When the merchant adds a new
specification, that approval becomes

23
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,078
outdated.

24
00:01:32,078 --> 00:01:37,500
The application requires a fresh
assessment before publication.

25
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,183
We add measured sleeve dimensions.

26
00:01:41,183 --> 00:01:48,341
A new assessment can disclose those
measurements and ask customers to check

27
00:01:48,341 --> 00:01:49,534
their device.

28
00:01:49,534 --> 00:01:55,500
Dimensions alone do not guarantee that
every sixteen-inch laptop fits.

29
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:01,677
Now the merchant reviews and approves the
new text.

30
00:02:01,677 --> 00:02:05,329
Publication creates a persistent page
version.

31
00:02:05,329 --> 00:02:12,631
We open the storefront, refresh it, and
read the published result back.

32
00:02:12,631 --> 00:02:17,500
Writing succeeded and content verification
are separate checks.

33
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:24,830
If a change needs to be reversed, the
merchant restores an earlier page.

34
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:27,380
Restoration creates another recorded
version.

35
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:33,500
The history remains visible, and the
restored content can be checked again.

36
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:40,121
The release passed five consecutive public
workflows and thirty-five local tests.

37
00:02:40,121 --> 00:02:44,965
The five journeys took twenty to sixty-
nine seconds.

38
00:02:44,965 --> 00:02:47,656
Earlier revisions had timeout failures.

39
00:02:47,656 --> 00:02:52,500
Human accuracy grading and merchant
testing are still pending.

40
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,373
Gemini runs through Vertex AI.

41
00:02:55,373 --> 00:02:59,719
Cloud Run serves the application,
Firestore records versions, and private

42
00:02:59,719 --> 00:03:01,892
Cloud Storage holds uploaded images.

43
00:03:01,892 --> 00:03:04,500
The model has no publishing tool.

44
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:11,118
Our next test is with merchants: can they
make accurate repairs with less effort?

45
00:03:11,118 --> 00:03:11,541
Pagemi.

46
00:03:11,541 --> 00:03:12,809
Fix the page.

47
00:03:12,809 --> 00:03:14,500
Not just the ticket.
